{%- comment -%}
  ===========================================================================
  SERVING REFERENCE — servings per package
  ===========================================================================

  Returns the number of FDA RACC servings contained in ONE package of a
  product. Used by snippets/product-card.liquid to turn a pack price into a
  per-serving price:

      per serving = variant price / (packages in variant x servings per package)

  Example — McFarland Springs Trout Dogs, 12-Pack at $260.00:
      26000 cents / (12 packages x 4 servings) = 541.67 -> $5.42 /serving

  Usage:
      {%- capture spp -%}
        {%- render 'serving-reference', handle: product.handle -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}

  Return values:
      1   (default) one package = one serving. Any handle not listed below
          behaves exactly as it did before this snippet existed, so an
          incomplete map is safe — never wrong, only less precise.
      2+  one package contains this many servings.
      0   SUPPRESS. Show no per-serving price at all; fall back to the normal
          price display. Use for anything sold by the jar or bottle where a
          per-serving figure is meaningless.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  HOW TO UPDATE
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The ops table below is the source of truth and is keyed by COMPONENT SKU.
  The storefront is keyed by PRODUCT HANDLE. These do not match — multi-pack
  variants get their own sequential SKUs (Trout Dogs single is
  SF-MCF-RBT-BLK-001, but the 12-Pack is SF-MCF-RBT-BLK-005), and Seatopia-
  branded duplicates are renumbered entirely (SF-SEA-RBT-BLK-004 is the same
  fish as SF-SIC-RBT-BLK-001). So the handle map has to be maintained by hand.

  To update: paste the refreshed ops table into the block below, then add or
  correct any handle in the case statement. Only rows with servings per
  package GREATER THAN 1 change what a customer sees.

