  NOTES ON THE SOURCE DATA (flagged 2026-08-07, not corrected here):
  1. HVF Furikake Lox has no COGS value.
  2. Caleta Steelhead Loin is named "(12oz)" but the package size column says
     10.00 oz. The 10.00 figure is what drives 2 servings at 5 oz.
  3. Three rows are internally inconsistent — package oz divided by servings
     does not equal the stated serving size:
       - Seacorp Half Shell: 16 oz / 1 serving, but serving size says 4 oz.
         If 4 oz is right this should be 4 servings, which would cut the
         displayed per-serving price by 75%. LEFT AT 1 pending confirmation.
       - Marshallberg Osetra: 1 oz / 2 servings = 0.5 oz, not 0.25 oz.
       - Yarra Valley Salmon Roe: same, 1 oz / 2 = 0.5 oz, not 0.25 oz.
         (30 g is ~1.06 oz; 0.25 oz servings would imply 4 per tin.)
     The servings column is what this file uses, so the serving-size column
     being wrong is harmless — but if SERVINGS is the wrong one, prices are
     wrong. Worth a look.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign spp = 1

  case handle

    comment
      -- 0 = SUPPRESS. No per-serving price at all; the card falls back to
         the normal price display.

         Condiments are bought by the jar or bottle. A "$0.69 /serving" on a
         garnish is noise, and the 20-servings figure in the ops table is a
         nutrition-label RACC, not a purchase decision. Their servings values
         are kept in the reference table above for costing purposes only.
    endcomment
    when 'kurotakesou-yuzu-kosho-4oz'
      assign spp = 0
    when 'yugeta-shoyu-4oz'
      assign spp = 0
    when 'dave-s-gourmet-pickled-ginger-4oz'
      assign spp = 0

    comment
      -- 4 servings per package --
    endcomment
    when 'black-tiger-shrimp-mangrove-regeneration'
      assign spp = 4
    when 'mcfarland-springs-trout-hot-dogs', 'mcfarland-springs-trout-dogs'
      assign spp = 4
    when 'scallop-meat-16oz', 'scallop-meat-regenerative-farmed-peruvian-scallops-no-shell-20-oz-bag-sunset'
      assign spp = 4

    comment
      -- 2 servings per package --
    endcomment
    when 'whole-trout-12oz', 'smoke-in-chimneys-whole-trout-12-16oz', 'smoke-in-chimneys-whole-trout-12oz'
      assign spp = 2
    when 'steelhead-sashimi-loin-12oz', 'caleta-bay-a-i-steelhead-loin-12oz'
      assign spp = 2
    when 'lab-tested-salmon-roe-caviar'
      assign spp = 2
    when 'marshallberg-classic-osetra-caviar'
      assign spp = 2

  endcase

  echo spp
-%}

